# GENERATED by desktop/themes/tools/generate.py from desktop/themes/colorschemes/Nexus.colors.in — DO NOT EDIT.
#
# NEXUS colour scheme for Qt/KDE applications and KWin window decorations
# (KColorScheme format). One template yields every variant:
#   Nexus{Dark,Light}.colors            default accent
#   Nexus{Dark,Light}<Accent>.colors    the other accents of the design system
#
# How the design tokens map to KDE's colour sets
#   Window         application chrome (menu bar, tool bars, dialogs, side panels) → bgSurface
#   View           content (lists, editors, input fields)                         → bgBase
#   Button         push buttons, combo boxes                                      → bgOverlay
#   Selection      highlight, progress, checked controls                          → accent
#   Tooltip        tool tips                                                      → bgOverlay
#   Header         title bar and the tool area merged with it                     → bgSurface
#   Complementary  dark "over the wallpaper" surfaces, in both modes              → dark bgBase
# so a third-party window has the same three levels as a NEXUS application:
# header and side areas on bgSurface, content on bgBase, raised controls above.

